## Topics

`email /` flow structures, timing and triggers, segmentation, deliverability, list
health, campaign calendar, design, benchmarks by stage.
`sms /` SMS strategy, consent and compliance, flows, RCS, SMS versus email role.

## The 9 flows

In build order: welcome, abandoned checkout, abandoned cart, browse abandon, post
purchase education, review request, replenishment, winback, VIP. 3 flows at the
smallest stage, the full set once a brand is established.

## Look for

Flow structures with message counts and exact timing. Trigger and exit conditions.
Segmentation rules. Email share of revenue benchmarks by stage. Authentication and
deliverability requirements, which are tier 1 platform material. For SMS: consent
rules by jurisdiction, frequency limits, and where SMS earns its higher cost per send.

## Skip

Subject line listicles. Tool tutorials that walk the Klaviyo interface without the
flow logic behind it: 1 full course is plenty, 3 is duplication. Email design
tutorials that are about Figma rather than about what converts.

## The underbuilt one

Post purchase education. Emails that get the customer to the outcome faster raise
repeat rate and cut returns at the same time, which is rare. Tie them to the job to be
done from 02-AVT, not to the product spec.

## The failure mode

Sending more and earning less. Prefer sources that treat engagement decay and
per-segment frequency caps as a hard limit on the calendar.

## Scope mix

Real baseline: authentication records set, welcome flow live, abandoned checkout flow
live, working unsubscribe, SMS consent captured correctly.

## Done when

All 9 flows specified message by message, with timing and conditions.

